@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Implemented          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L110)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L142), [validated by: redacts values from logs and results on validation failure](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L217)).
+- Rejection messages and log lines name failing property paths using dot notation for nested fields ([validated by: formats nested property paths in validation errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L281)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes through extra properties unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L89)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws for unregistered tool names](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L183)).
+
+## Registry metadata retrieval
+
+- `ToolRegistry.getPromptInstructions` returns a list of formatted instructions from all registered tools that declare `promptInstructions` ([validated by: provides prompt instructions from all registered tools](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L41)).
+- `ToolRegistry.getExamplePrompts` returns a flattened list of all example prompts from all registered tools ([validated by: provides example prompts from all registered tools](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L65)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94), [validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L169)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles static schema once at register time](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L188)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: caches compiled validators for function-valued tool definitions by schema reference](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L8), [validated by: validates against the current schema for function-valued definitions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L252)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112), [validated by: retries a tool call when the first attempt is rejected by the registry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L523)).
